    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498-a1">

                <pb facs="0564" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg544"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office U.S. Military Telegraph</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">War Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 15, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The following telegram was received at Washington 5.50 p. m., from San Francisco,
                    October 14, 1864:</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kanagawa, September</hi> 2, 1864.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The ambassadors who made the French
                    convention have been disgraced; convention repudiated; combined fleet gone to
                    destroy batteries at Simonoseki.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
